course: dictionary
lesson: 14030
title: Mammalian features
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mammalian is a long word for something you already know. It means "to do with mammals", or having the features of a mammal. Mammals are animals with hair or fur, and mothers feed their babies on milk.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «Mammalian features include hair, warm blood, and feeding babies with milk.» These clues tell you that mammalian is about the features that mammals have.
explain: Scientists use mammalian in textbooks and documentaries because it sounds more formal. «The forest has many mammalian species, such as foxes, deer and bats.» Swap in the word "mammal" and the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: Mammals are animals with hair or fur, warm blood, and young that feed on their mother's milk.
fact: «Mammalian» means to do with mammals, or having the features of a mammal.
fact: Humans, dogs, whales and bats are all mammals.
fact: Birds are not mammals: they have feathers and lay eggs with hard shells.
fact: A good check is to swap in the word "mammal" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Mammalian features include hair and milk for babies.» What does mammalian mean here? | *Of mammals | Of rocks | Of fish | Of plants
exercise: «The scientist studied mammalian cells under the microscope.» Which group of animals do the cells belong to? | Birds | *Mammals | Fish | Frogs
exercise: Which of these is a mammalian feature? | Feathers | Scales | A hard shell | *Hair or fur
test: «Whales are mammalian, so they breathe air and feed their babies milk.» What does mammalian mean here? | Made of metal | Able to fly | *Belonging to mammals | Belonging to plants
test: Which word means "of mammals"? | Reptilian | Avian | *Mammalian
exam: Which one is NOT a mammalian feature? | Hair or fur | *Laying hard shelled eggs | Warm blood | Feeding young on milk
